1280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 326 0 R
/T (This project provides a data-driven view of retail demand by combining exploratory analysis, feature engineering, predictive modeling, model evaluation, and explainability. The findings highlight how historical demand, inventory levels, ordering activity, promotions, seasonality, and weather conditions contribute to demand prediction across products, stores, and regions. Model evaluation further demonstrates that predictive performance varies across demand levels and product categories, with unusually high-demand events remaining more challenging to capture accurately. The project establishes a foundation for extending retail demand intelligence through advanced forecasting methods, improved time-series features, model optimization, and scenario-based inventory planning.)
/E (This project provides a data-driven view of retail demand by combining exploratory analysis, feature engineering, predictive modeling, model evaluation, and explainability. The findings highlight how historical demand, inventory levels, ordering activity, promotions, seasonality, and weather conditions contribute to demand prediction across products, stores, and regions. Model evaluation further demonstrates that predictive performance varies across demand levels and product categories, with unusually high-demand events remaining more challenging to capture accurately. The project establishes a foundation for extending retail demand intelligence through advanced forecasting methods, improved time-series features, model optimization, and scenario-based inventory planning.)
/Pg 70 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
